The timer is set as if the turn on lent time were the thread's own.
It lets pass the ticks at which another thread may pay for the turn, or none.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets a tick pass while the turn runs on lent time

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -893,9 +893,6 @@ uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
         return wake;
     }
     /* Each tick decides afresh who pays for a turn on lent time, and whether it has any. */
-    if (core->payer != NULL) {
-        return 1;
-    }
     /* A thread that lost the time of this core during its turn here, its place emptied, ends the turn at the next tick. */
     const struct place *p = thread_place_on(turn, core_index());
     if (core->run_queue != 0 || p == NULL) {
